## Understanding BOLA/IDOR with UUIDs
A BOLA/IDOR vulnerability occurs when an API endpoint handles database queries by relying entirely on user-supplied resource identifiers without validating if the logged-in user actually owns that data.

* Simple ID (Vulnerable): https://target.com (Easy to guess by incrementing to 1002).
* UUID Protection: To stop guessing attacks, modern developers switch to Universally Unique Identifiers (UUIDs), which look like this: api/v1/invoice?id=4a2b8e12-70fc-4638-b789-9a2c3d4e5f6g.

Because a standard UUIDv4 is randomly generated out of 2¹²⁸ combinations, brute-forcing them blindly is impossible. To find a BOLA bug on a UUID-protected endpoint, you must use smart leakage tracking techniques.
